## SEC chairman statement, July 8, 2019 (WebFetch 2026-11-09)
URL: https://www.sec.gov/newsroom/speeches-statements/clayton-regulation-best-interest-investment-adviser-fiduciary-duty
- The investment adviser fiduciary duty is "comprised of both a duty of care and a duty of loyalty"; it requires advisers always to act in the client's best interest.
- Regulation Best Interest "imposes a new standard of conduct specifically for broker-dealers", requiring them to act in the "best interest of their retail customers" with four component obligations: Disclosure, Care, Conflict of Interest, Compliance.

